⍝ Add.tc
⍝ ═══════

⍝@ test4.

      ⎕IO←1

      ⍝ Precond: A and B numeric
      ⍝ inv: A+B ←→ B+A   (+ is commutative, even when the sum
      ⍝ overflows int64 and is promoted to float)
      A ← ⎕RVAL 1 (,5) (,0 1 0 0 0)
      B ← ⎕RVAL 1 (,5) (,0 1 0 0 0)
      (A+B) ≡ B+A
1
      A ← ⎕RVAL 2 (3 4) (,0 0 1 0 0)
      B ← ⎕RVAL 2 (3 4) (,0 0 1 0 0)
      (A+B) ≡ B+A
1

      ⍝ Precond: Big sits at the int64 boundary so that Big+Small
      ⍝ always overflows and is promoted to float
      ⍝ (Cell::sum_overflow(), IntCell::bif_add_ii()); Small is small
      ⍝ enough to be exactly double-representable, so subtracting it
      ⍝ back out of the float sum is exact
      ⍝ inv: Big ←→ (Big+Small)-Small
      ⍝ (the reverse recovery, Small ←→ (Big+Small)-Big, is NOT exact:
      ⍝ converting the huge Big to a double already loses precision on
      ⍝ its own, independently of the addition - so it is not tested)
      Small ← 1+999∣|⎕RVAL 0
      Big ← 9223372036854775807
      Big ≡ (Big+Small)-Small
1
      Small ← ¯1-999∣|⎕RVAL 0
      Big ← ¯9223372036854775808
      Big ≡ (Big+Small)-Small
1
